alues:\r\n\r\n   * Demo Visa ending in 4242.\r\n   * Demo MasterCard ending in 4444.\r\n3. Do not ask users to enter genuine card numbers, CVVs or banking credentials.\r\n4. Simulate:\r\n\r\n   * Validating test details.\r\n   * Authorising payment.\r\n   * Payment approved.\r\n5. Send only the selected method, plan and customer email to the backend.\r\n6. Never transmit or store card-number, expiry or CVV fields.\r\n\r\nFASTAPI BACKEND\r\n\r\nAdd appropriate endpoints such as:\r\n\r\n* GET `/api/session`\r\n* POST `/api/demo-payment`\r\n* POST `/api/logout`\r\n\r\nThe demonstration payment endpoint must:\r\n\r\n1. Accept only `ecocash`, `visa` or `mastercard`.\r\n2. Validate the email and selected plan.\r\n3. Generate a unique demonstration transaction reference.\r\n4. Return an approved demonstration-payment response.\r\n5. Log a structured event containing:\r\n\r\n   * Demonstration transaction reference.\r\n   * Payment method.\r\n   * Plan.\r\n   * Timestamp.\r\n   * Status.\r\n6. Never log or store mobile numbers, card numbers, expiry dates, CVVs or other financial credentials.\r\n\r\nDEMO-PAID SESSION\r\n\r\nAfter a successful simulated payment:\r\n\r\n1. Create a signed membership-access session.\r\n2. Store it in a secure HTTP-only cookie rather than localStorage.\r\n3. Use a `DEMO_SESSION_SECRET` environment variable to sign the session.\r\n4. Configure the cookie with:\r\n\r\n   * HttpOnly.\r\n   * SameSite=Lax.\r\n   * Secure when deployed through HTTPS.\r\n   * A reasonable demonstration expiry.\r\n5. Redirect the user to `/library`.\r\n\r\nACCESS CONTROL\r\n\r\n1. Move or route the existing catalogue interface to `/library`.\r\n2. Only a valid demo-paid session may access `/library`.\r\n3. Unpaid users attempting to open `/library` must be redirected to the landing or checkout page.\r\n4. Protect these existing endpoints using a reusable FastAPI dependency:\r\n\r\n   * `/api/media`\r\n   * `/api/media/{media_id}`\r\n   * `/api/play-events`\r\n5. Keep `/api/health` and `/docs` publicly accessible for assessment.\r\n6. When a paid session is active:\r\n\r\n   * Show the customer email or “Demo Member”.\r\n   * Show a “Sign Out” button.\r\n   * Allow catalogue browsing.\r\n   * Allow music samples.\r\n   * Allow the five-second movie preview.\r\n7. Signing out must clear the membership cookie and return the user to the landing page.\r\n8. Add a clearly labelled “Reset Demonstration” control for assessment purposes.\r\n\r\nIMPORTANT LIMITATION\r\n\r\nThe current video and audio samples may remain public static demonstration assets. Do not claim that this prototype provides DRM or fully secure commercial media protection. Document that a production system would require private object storage, authenticated delivery URLs and digital-rights controls.\r\n\r\nTESTS\r\n\r\nAdd automated tests covering:\r\n\r\n* Landing page is publicly accessible.\r\n* Checkout page is publicly accessible.\r\n* Unpaid user cannot access `/library`.\r\n* Unpaid user cannot retrieve protected catalogue data.\r\n* Invalid payment method is rejected.\r\n* Invalid email is rejected.\r\n* Successful EcoCash simulation.\r\n* Successful Visa simulation.\r\n* Successful MasterCard simulation.\r\n* Successful simulation sets an access cookie.\r\n* Demo-paid user can open `/library`.\r\n* Demo-paid user can access catalogue endpoints.\r\n* Logout clears access.\r\n* Existing catalogue, filtering, music and movie-preview tests continue to pass.\r\n\r\nRun all tests and fix every failure. Finish by reporting files changed, endpoints added, actual test results and remaining limitations. Do not report success without testing.\r\n\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-08-25T21:06:37+02:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":181,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T19:06:37Z","thinking":"**Analyzing Architecture Details**\n\nI'm currently diving into the architectural overview and requirements for the StreamWave serverless platform. Focusing on the need to extend the FastAPI/Vercel project, I'm identifying key areas for expansion and integration. The goal is a clear understanding before proceeding with further development.\n\n\n**Designing Landing Page Elements**\n\nI've been working on the public-facing landing page, specifically the `/` route. My focus is on the hero section: crafting compelling text (\"Zimbabwe's stories, music, and movies - all in one place\") and incorporating the StreamWave logo. I want a clean, professional UI, avoiding generic AI-generated designs. I'm also ensuring the \"Sign In\" button, email field, and \"Get Started\" button are prominently placed. I've designed a clear structure for the benefits and \"How it works\" sections. I am also planning the simulated checkout page at `/checkout`.\n\n\n**Implementing Payment Simulation**\n\nI'm now implementing the Visa/MasterCard simulation. My recent progress involves defining demo cards with masked values, simulating payment authorization, and ensuring only essential data (`method`, `plan_id`/`plan_name`, `email`) is sent to the backend. Card details are never transmitted or stored. I'm focusing on a seamless user experience for the demo payment flow.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"list_dir","args":{"DirectoryPath":"C:\\Users\\dell\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457","toolAction":"Listing workspace files","toolSummary":"Listing workspace files"}}]}
