{"step_index":193,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T19:08:36Z","thinking":"**Considering Security Options**\n\nI'm currently weighing security implementation choices. It's a question of utilizing the `itsdangerous` library, which is already integrated within the Pallets ecosystem, or developing a custom HMAC-SHA256 session token serializer. I'm leaning toward the standard library approach. I'm focusing on `hmac`, `hashlib`, `base64`, `json`, and `time`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Security Design**\n\nI've determined that `base64` is preferable due to its lack of dependencies and compatibility with Vercel serverless functions. I've formulated a simple session token structure: base64-encoded JSON payload concatenated with a base64-encoded HMAC-SHA256 signature. Verification involves decoding, recomputing the HMAC, and checking expiration via `hmac.compare_digest`. I'm setting an `httponly`, `samesite`, and `secure` cookie.\n\n\n**Implementing Access Control**\n\nI'm now implementing the access control logic, constructing a `verify_paid_session` FastAPI dependency. This dependency checks for the presence and validity of the `streamwave_session` cookie, decoding it and verifying its integrity. I'm raising HTTP exceptions for missing or invalid sessions, and using the dependency to protect the media endpoints: `/api/media`, `/api/media/{media_id}`, and `/api/play-events`. Unprotected endpoints include `/api/health`, `/api/session`, `/api/demo-payment`, `/api/logout`, and `/api/reset-demo`, along with documentation and static HTML routes.\n\n\n**Designing Checkout Functionality**\n\nI'm now designing the checkout process and payment simulation. My focus is on creating a user-friendly experience that mirrors a real transaction without processing any actual payments. I'm prioritizing clarity, ensuring that all demonstration elements are clearly marked as such to avoid any confusion for the user. I'm focusing on the `/checkout` page, specifically how the EcoCash and Visa/Mastercard options are presented.\n\nI'm making sure that the page automatically populates with the user's email, and uses simulation payment flows that are smooth for the user.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Implementation Plan for StreamWave Landing Page, EcoCash/Visa/MasterCard Academic Payment Simulation, and Cookie-Based Paid Member Access Control.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Implementation Plan - StreamWave Landing Page, Simulated Checkout & Paid Member Access Control\n\nExtend the existing **StreamWave Entertainment** FastAPI serverless application on Vercel by adding an original public landing page, simulated subscription-payment checkout (EcoCash, Visa, MasterCard), signed cookie session management, and protected member access control for `/library`.\n\n---\n\n## User Review Required\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Academic Simulation Safety**: This is a non-commercial academic demonstration. No real money will be transferred and no actual financial information (card numbers, CVVs, PINs, mobile payment PINs) will be collected, transmitted, or logged.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Access Control Model**: Catalogue browsing (`/api/media`), detail lookups (`/api/media/{id}`), and playback event logging (`/api/play-events`) will be protected by FastAPI signed session cookies. The `/api/health` and `/docs` endpoints remain publicly accessible for automated assessment checks.\n\n---\n\n## Proposed Changes\n\n### Configuration & Central Subscription Settings\n\n#### [MODIFY] [`app.py`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/app.py)\n- Define a single subscription configuration source of truth:\n  ```python\n  SUBSCRIPTION_PLAN = {\n      \"id\": \"streamwave-monthly\",\n      \"name\": \"StreamWave Monthly\",\n      \"price\": \"US$2.99\",\n      \"price_amount\": 2.99,\n      \"currency\": \"USD\",\n      \"interval\": \"month\"\n  }\n  ```\n- Implement secure session cookie signature logic using `DEMO_SESSION_SECRET` env var with a fallback.\n- Implement FastAPI reusable dependency `verify_paid_session` to protect `/api/media`, `/api/media/{media_id}`, and `/api/play-events`.\n- Add new endpoints:\n  - `GET /api/session`: Checks active session cookie status.\n  - `POST /api/demo-payment`: Validates email, plan, and payment method (`ecocash`, `visa`, `mastercard`), generates reference `SW-DEMO-XXXXX`, logs structured JSON event, and sets `streamwave_session` HTTP-only cookie.\n  - `POST /api/logout`: Clears session cookie.\n  - `POST /api/reset-demo`: Reset control endpoint for assessment.\n  - `GET /`: Serves landing page `public/index.html`.\n  - `GET /checkout`: Serves checkout page `public/checkout.html`.\n  - `GET /library`: Serves member library catalogue `public/library.html`.\n\n---\n\n### User Interface & Static Pages\n\n#### [MODIFY] [`public/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/index.html)\n- Transform into the **Public Landing Page** (`/`):\n  - StreamWave Logo and Sign In button.\n  - Original Hero section using StreamWave artwork with dark overlay.\n  - Copy:\n    - Heading: *\"Zimbabwe’s stories, music and movies — all in one place.\"*\n    - Supporting text: *\"Stream from US$2.99 per month. Cancel anytime.\"*\n    - Instruction: *\"Enter your email address to start your StreamWave membership.\"*\n  - Email input & **Get Started** button redirecting to `/checkout?email=...`.\n  - Benefits section, \"How It Works\" section, Supported payment methods section (EcoCash, Visa, MasterCard), and academic footer.\n\n#### [NEW] [`public/checkout.html`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/checkout.html)\n- Create the **Checkout Page** (`/checkout`):\n  - Prominent banner: *\"ACADEMIC PAYMENT SIMULATION — No real money will be charged. Do not enter genuine payment information.\"*\n  - Customer email input & subscription summary ($2.99/mo).\n  - Three simulated payment method tabs:\n    1. **EcoCash**: Displays prefilled test number `077 000 0000`, step animation (*Sending request...* -> *Waiting for mobile confirmation...* -> *Approved*).\n    2. **Visa**: Displays masked test card ending in `4242`, step animation (*Validating test details...* -> *Authorising...* -> *Approved*).\n    3. **MasterCard**: Displays masked test card ending in `4444`, step animation (*Validating test details...* -> *Authorising...* -> *Approved*).\n  - Submits simulation to `POST /api/demo-payment`, receives signed cookie, and redirects to `/library`.\n\n#### [NEW] [`public/library.html`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/library.html)\n- Create the **Paid Member Catalogue Page** (`/library`):\n  - Protected catalogue grid, search bar, genre/type filters, HTML5 audio player bar for music, and 5-second MP4 movie preview modal.\n  - Member status bar showing customer email, **Sign Out** button, and **Reset Demonstration** control.\n  - Redirects unpaid visitors to `/checkout` or `/` if no valid session cookie is present.\n\n#### [MODIFY] [`public/css/styles.css`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/css/styles.css)\n- Add landing page section styles, checkout step animation styles, test card tab styles, and member library navigation styling.\n\n#### [MODIFY] [`public/js/app.js`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/public/js/app.js)\n- Implement checkout simulation frontend handlers, EcoCash/Visa/MasterCard step sequences, session verification API calls, and sign-out logic.\n\n---\n\n### Test Suite Updates\n\n#### [MODIFY] [`tests/test_api.py`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/tests/test_api.py)\n- Add test coverage for:\n  - Public landing page (`/`) accessibility.\n  - Public checkout page (`/checkout`) accessibility.\n  - Rejection of unpaid users on `/api/media` (HTTP 401).\n  - Validation errors for invalid emails or payment methods (HTTP 422).\n  - Successful EcoCash simulation setting `streamwave_session` cookie.\n  - Successful Visa and MasterCard simulations.\n  - Paid member access to `/api/media` and `/api/play-events`.\n  - Sign out clearing session cookie.\n  - 100% regression verification of existing search, filter, music, and movie preview tests.\n\n---\n\n## Verification Plan\n\n### Automated Tests\nRun pytest in Windows Command Prompt:\n```cmd\npytest tests\\test_api.py -v\n```\n\n### Manual Verification\n1. Open `http://127.0.0.1:8001/` -> Confirm landing page heading *\"Zimbabwe’s stories, music and movies — all in one place.\"*\n2. Enter email `test@streamwave.co.zw` and click **Get Started** -> Redirects to `/checkout?email=test@streamwave.co.zw`.\n3. Test EcoCash simulation on `/checkout` -> Observe step animation, verify HTTP-only cookie set, redirect to `/library`.\n4. Browse catalogue on `/library`, test 5-second movie preview and music audio player.\n5. Test **Sign Out** -> Confirms cookie cleared and redirects to landing page `/`.\n6. Verify unpaid direct access to `/api/media` returns HTTP 401 Unauthorized.\n","Description":"Create implementation plan for landing page, checkout simulation, and session access control","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\dell\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\\implementation_plan.md","toolAction":"Creating implementation plan","toolSummary":"Creating implementation plan"}}]}
